# Test: a spec author runs le spec design documents and le spec design check on a spec and reads the owed rows
# QUESTION: does the registered `le spec design` area, typed as an author
#   types it, derive the design pages and the decision row a spec's file
#   links, and refuse a Design documents table that omits them, naming each
#   owed row, the judge step and the command that lists the rows?
# WHY NOT A UNIT TEST: TestDesignDocumentsDerivation and TestDesignCheckJudgement
#   call derive and checkSpec in process; this proves the actions are
#   registered in le, that their grammar reaches answerDocuments and
#   answerCheck, and that the exit codes and the text reach the author through
#   the real binary.
# VALIDATES: spec-design-needs-owner-approval AC-13 and AC-14 (a missing page
#   row, a missing decision row, no judge approval, the clean table owing only
#   the judge), through the real entry point.
# Exercises: answerDocuments -> derive -> DeclaredDesignDocuments,
#   DocumentsByPath, doorindex.Load -> addDecisions; answerCheck -> checkSpec
#   -> missingRows, judgeRow, presentationProblems, judgeApprovalProblem.
# The checkout is the test's own directory: a non-harness le step runs at the
#   repository root, so design.sh points le at this directory through
#   ZE_REPO_ROOT, and the tmpfs files below form the whole checkout (the two
#   root markers, the system door, one source file whose // Design: header
#   names a page with one decision row, a second page anchored to the file,
#   the record the row cites, and two fix specs). No judge record exists, so
#   both checks owe the judge.

option=timeout:value=120s

tmpfs=repo/go.mod:terminator=EOF_GOMOD
module example.com/design-fixture
EOF_GOMOD

tmpfs=repo/feature-gates.txt:terminator=EOF_GATES
# the second root marker le looks for
EOF_GATES

tmpfs=repo/ai/doors/system.md:terminator=EOF_DOOR
# System door

<!-- door-base: pkg cmd/ze internal -->
EOF_DOOR

tmpfs=repo/internal/component/widget/widget.yang:terminator=EOF_YANG
// Design: docs/architecture/widget.md -- the widget

module widget {
}
EOF_YANG

tmpfs=repo/docs/architecture/widget.md:terminator=EOF_PAGE
# Widget

How the widget answers.

## Design decisions

| Decision | It forbids | Source | Date |
|---|---|---|---|
| The widget answers data and the surface renders it | Rendering text in the widget | plan/records/widget.md | 2026-08-21 |
EOF_PAGE

tmpfs=repo/docs/architecture/widget-flow.md:terminator=EOF_FLOW
# Widget flow

The answer travels from the widget to the surface.
<!-- source: internal/component/widget/widget.yang -- widget -->
EOF_FLOW

tmpfs=repo/plan/records/widget.md:terminator=EOF_RECORD
# Widget record
EOF_RECORD

tmpfs=repo/plan/release/fixes/spec-widget.md:terminator=EOF_SPEC
# Spec: widget

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| Status | design |
| Priority | P2 |
| Updated | 2026-11-20 |

## Task

Render the widget in the surface.

## Acceptance Criteria

| AC ID | Input | Expected |
|---|---|---|
| AC-1 | a widget | the surface renders it |

## Files to Modify
- `internal/component/widget/widget.yang` - render in the surface

## Design documents

| Document | Section | Derived from | Binding statement | Verdict | How this design stands against it |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `ai/doors/system.md` | System door | every change | - | silent | The door names no rule on rendering |
| `docs/architecture/widget-flow.md` | Widget flow | anchored to the file | - | silent | The page describes the path, not who renders |

## Design presentation

### What changes

The surface renders the widget.

### Before and after

Before: the widget renders text. After: the surface renders it.

### Alternatives set aside

Rendering in the widget, which the decision forbids.

### Documents departed from

none

### Choices for Thomas

None.

## Implementation Steps

1. Render.
EOF_SPEC

tmpfs=repo/plan/release/fixes/spec-widget-whole.md:terminator=EOF_WHOLE
# Spec: widget whole

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| Status | design |
| Priority | P2 |
| Updated | 2026-11-20 |

## Task

Render the widget in the surface.

## Acceptance Criteria

| AC ID | Input | Expected |
|---|---|---|
| AC-1 | a widget | the surface renders it |

## Files to Modify
- `internal/component/widget/widget.yang` - render in the surface

## Design documents

| Document | Section | Derived from | Binding statement | Verdict | How this design stands against it |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `docs/architecture/widget.md` | Design decisions | Design header of the file | "The widget answers data and the surface renders it" | agrees | The surface renders |
| `docs/architecture/widget-flow.md` | Widget flow | anchored to the file | - | silent | The page describes the path, not who renders |
| `ai/doors/system.md` | System door | every change | - | silent | The door names no rule on rendering |

## Design presentation

### What changes

The surface renders the widget.

### Before and after

Before: the widget renders text. After: the surface renders it.

### Alternatives set aside

Rendering in the widget, which the decision forbids.

### Documents departed from

none

### Choices for Thomas

None.

## Implementation Steps

1. Render.
EOF_WHOLE

# The derivation: the system door, the header page, the anchored page, and the decision row.
cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=le test fixture spec/design-in-dir repo 0 documents spec plan/release/fixes/spec-widget.md:exit=0
expect=stdout:contains=plan/release/fixes/spec-widget.md: 3 design pages, 1 decision rows owe a verdict in ## Design documents
expect=stdout:contains=  ai/doors/system.md  (the door every change reads
expect=stdout:contains=  docs/architecture/widget.md  (the // Design: page of internal/component/widget/widget.yang)
expect=stdout:contains=  docs/architecture/widget-flow.md  (anchored to internal/component/widget/widget.yang)
expect=stdout:contains=  docs/architecture/widget.md, Design decisions, decision of 2026-08-21: "The widget answers data and the surface renders it"

# A table that omits the header page and its decision row owes both, then the judge.
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=le test fixture spec/design-in-dir repo 1 check spec plan/release/fixes/spec-widget.md:exit=1
expect=stdout:contains=spec-widget.md: ## Design documents is missing 2 rows owed by its files
expect=stdout:contains=  - docs/architecture/widget.md  (the // Design: page of internal/component/widget/widget.yang)
expect=stdout:contains=  - docs/architecture/widget.md, Design decisions, decision of 2026-08-21: "The widget answers data and the surface renders it"
expect=stdout:contains=spec-widget.md: no judge has judged this design; fix: have ze-design-judge judge it
expect=stdout:contains=run ./le spec design documents spec plan/release/fixes/spec-widget.md to list the owed rows

# The whole table owes only the judge.
cmd=foreground:seq=3:exec=le test fixture spec/design-in-dir repo 1 check spec plan/release/fixes/spec-widget-whole.md:exit=1
expect=stdout:contains=spec-widget-whole.md: no judge has judged this design; fix: have ze-design-judge judge it
expect=stdout:contains=run ./le spec design documents spec plan/release/fixes/spec-widget-whole.md to list the owed rows
reject=stdout:contains=is missing
reject=stdout:contains=verbatim span
reject=stdout:contains=; fix: write it
